" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304809 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304809 #edb/ref 1071 "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304809 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f297359-1573-550c-acfb-39ada6af0bec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304809 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+1\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $-1$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $3$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304812 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304812 #edb/ref 1069 "q-330302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304812 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304812 #edb/ref 1071 "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304812 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6d8d0be-fe4e-5e1a-948d-b8eb21d680a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304812 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)={x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{{x}_{1}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option III is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342856 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{2t} \\\\ 4{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342856 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342856 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b46262a-ea6e-57a1-8406-66175333482d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343170 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{t} \\\\ 9{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343170 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343170 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6ce1c0e6-e2e6-502e-9f4c-424926b822b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343249 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343249 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343249 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "74e589ed-48ac-59f0-91f5-306d48ff8612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343526 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}18{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343526 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343526 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "93608c1a-4041-5e25-aa59-46c3bd8517da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343607 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{t} \\\\ 4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343607 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343607 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9b2edceb-8a29-5479-8a92-b9e45a47b032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186343607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344842 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c8770828-84f3-5d0f-8bac-379001547362" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345233 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345233 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345233 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345233 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\,u(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,v(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$, find $Aw(t)$ where $w(t)=[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345233 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "230cd2b1-a961-52f2-a633-edc5837452c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345233 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $u(t)$ and $v(t)$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ the superposition principle guarantees that \n\n$$\ncu(t)+dv(t)\n$$\n\n is also a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for all $c,d\\in R.$\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\nw(t)=9u(t)+2v(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $w$ is a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ So, in order to find $Aw(t)$ we just need to find ${w}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Aw & ={w}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(9{e}^{t})^{′} \\\\ (2{e}^{2t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{t} \\\\ 4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393660 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393660 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76602" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393660 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393660 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\,u(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,v(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$, find $Aw(t)$ where $w(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-4{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -6{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393660 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4f6678b6-2c25-5e0a-b02d-0f73823bf62a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393660 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $u(t)$ and $v(t)$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ the superposition principle guarantees that \n\n$$\ncu(t)+dv(t)\n$$\n\n is also a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for all $c,d\\in R.$\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\nw(t)=-4u(t)-6v(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $w$ is a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ So, in order to find $Aw(t)$ we just need to find ${w}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Aw & ={w}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-4{e}^{-5t})^{′} \\\\ (-6{e}^{-3t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 18{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393661 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "61e343c4-069d-53a1-b0f9-8f120b5523a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393662 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}20{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 18{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393662 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393662 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46984b47-2c2e-5d5e-8853-8d21152030c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393663 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}20{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 18{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393663 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393663 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2796b883-2354-5261-8fe3-d13f5316591d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393664 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}30{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 12{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393664 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393664 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3692dee3-45b9-5922-9e52-0a000ffdd1e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393665 #edb/ref 1080 "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}30{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 12{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393665 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393665 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa019a90-c433-550f-bc4a-49f7196227df" #edb/ref 175921